{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrqua1iYfP4CAKBuqwps","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"<REDACTED>","signature":""},{"type":"server_tool_use","id":"srvtoolu_01XwKNeBJaDDo5m9j5dhsRPV","name":"web_search","input":{"query":"Claude Code overview documentation Anthropic"}},{"type":"web_search_tool_result","tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XwKNeBJaDDo5m9j5dhsRPV","content":[{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Claude Code Official Documentation by Anthropic","url":"https://claudelog.com/faqs/claude-code-docs/","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"412 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"claude-code-analysis/DOCUMENTATION.md at main · ComeOnOliver/claude-code-analysis","url":"https://github.com/ComeOnOliver/claude-code-analysis/blob/main/DOCUMENTATION.md","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"192 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Overview - Claude Code Docs","url":"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/overview","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"592 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"GitHub - anthropics/claude-code: Claude Code is an agentic coding tool that lives in your terminal, understands your codebase, and helps you code faster by executing routine tasks, explaining complex code, and handling git workflows - all through natural language commands. · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"6 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"The Claude Code Handbook: A Professional Introduction to Building with AI-Assisted Development","url":"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/claude-code-handbook/","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"197 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Overview - Claude Code Docs","url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/overview","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"86 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Claude Code by Anthropic","url":"https://claude.com/product/claude-code","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"7 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Documentation - Claude Platform Docs","url":"https://platform.claude.com/docs","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"69 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Claude Code","url":"https://aiagentindex.mit.edu/2025/claude-code","encrypted_content":"","page_age":null}],"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"<REDACTED>","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I searched for this, and the official overview page now appears to live at code.claude.com. Anthropic's GitHub repo for Claude Code links to "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"code.claude.com/docs/en/overview"},{"type":"text","text":". The older address, "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/overview"},{"type":"text","text":", still shows up in results and on community sites like ClaudeLog.\n\n**What Claude Code is**\n- The overview page calls it "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"an agentic coding tool that reads your codebase, edits files, runs commands, and works with your development tools. You can use it in a terminal, an IDE, a desktop app or a browser."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"It helps you build features, fix bugs and automate development tasks. It can work across many files and tools because it understands your whole codebase."},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**Where it runs and what you need**\n- The docs have setup tabs for "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"Terminal, VS Code, Desktop app, Web, and JetBrains"},{"type":"text","text":".\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"Most of these need a Claude subscription or an Anthropic Console account. The terminal, VS Code and JetBrains versions also work with third-party providers."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"The VS Code extension shows inline diffs, @-mentions, plan review and conversation history inside the editor."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"The browser version needs no local setup."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- The GitHub README says you can also "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"tag @claude on GitHub"},{"type":"text","text":".\n\n**Installing and first run**\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"The native installer is the recommended option, and Homebrew is also supported."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"WinGet installs don't update themselves, so you need to run `winget upgrade Anthropic.ClaudeCode` from time to time."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"You can also install it with apt, dnf or apk on Debian, Fedora, RHEL and Alpine."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- To start, open a project folder and run `claude`. "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"It asks you to log in the first time, unless you've set the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY environment variable and approve using it."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- After that, the docs point to "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"a Quickstart that walks through a first real task, from exploring a codebase to committing a fix, plus a guide to giving Claude lasting instructions and memories."},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**From the product page (claude.com)**\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"Claude Pro and Max plans include Claude Code."},{"type":"text","text":" It's "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"available for macOS, Linux, and Windows"},{"type":"text","text":".\n- Use cases it highlights:\n  - "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"mapping out whole codebases with agentic search, so you don't have to pick context files yourself"},{"type":"text","text":"\n  - "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"working with GitHub, GitLab and command-line tools to turn issues into tested pull requests"},{"type":"text","text":"\n  - "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"refactors and migrations that run for hours"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**Other resources**\n- The Claude Platform docs at platform.claude.com also link to Claude Code, "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"calling it an agentic coding assistant in your terminal"},{"type":"text","text":".\n- Unofficial guides include ClaudeLog, which "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"adds practical workflows and tips tested by the community"},{"type":"text","text":", and freeCodeCamp's Claude Code Handbook. There's also an unofficial GitHub repo with "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"a reverse-engineered analysis of how the source code is built"},{"type":"text","text":". Anthropic didn't make any of these."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5945,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4510},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":1,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null}